## Table 3 the definition question

This is the high-value short answer. The best-supported public-domain “yes” is **CDC 1998**, which published pediatric **hematocrit** cutoffs alongside hemoglobin. WHO’s current public carrier is **hemoglobin-only**. The current NHLBI/AAP materials I found treat hematocrit as part of a CBC or screening workflow, but do **not** publish pediatric hematocrit diagnostic cutoffs as the anemia definition. ASH’s review article is the closest society-adjacent source I found; it says pediatric anemia is defined in practice by low **Hb, Hct, or RBC count** relative to age/sex ranges, but it is not a formal society cutoff table. citeturn47search1turn45search1turn46search1turn45search0turn46search3

