|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| WHO | no | none | `<5 y` Hb-only on public carrier | WHO 2026; `https://www.who.int/data/nutrition/nlis/info/anaemia` | public-domain | “Anaemia is defined as a haemoglobin concentration below a specified cut-off point.” |
| CDC | yes | 1-<2 y: `<32.9 %`; 2-<5 y: `<33.0 %`; 5-<8 y: `<34.5 %`; 8-<12 y: `<35.4 %`; male 12-<15 y: `<37.3 %`; male 15-<18 y: `<39.7 %`; female 12-<15 y: `<35.7 %`; female 15-<18 y: `<35.9 %` | 6 months-<18 y, with note that 1-<2 y values can be used for infants 6-12 months | CDC MMWR 1998; `https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/00051880.htm` | public-domain | Table 6: “Maximum hemoglobin concentration and hematocrit values for anemia.” |
